# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# This repository is public, and the thing it is built to produce is a
# recording of somebody's life. The rule is that nothing derived from a real
# archive goes in it: not the audio, not the transcripts, not the voiceprints,
# not a screenshot of the interface with real names on the screen.
#
# Everything below the first heading is that rule. The rest is ordinary build
# and tooling noise.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# secrets
.env
.env.*
*.key
*.pem
secrets.json
data/secrets.json

# recordings, transcripts, and voiceprints of real people — never commit
data/
*.wav
*.mp3
*.m4a
*.opus
*.flac
*.raw

# the archive's own databases and derived stores
*.db
*.db-wal
*.db-shm
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
*.jsonl

# screenshots of the running interface.
#
# A UI screenshot is a transcript. `people-tab.png` sat in this repository
# showing the real enrolled voices -- names, sample counts, the clip each
# reference came from. Staged demo captures are welcome, and they live in
# docs/ and are added deliberately with `git add -f`.
*.png
*.jpg
*.jpeg
*.gif
*.webp
!docs/*.jpg
!docs/*.png

# anything a tool captured from the live system
.playwright-mcp/
.codex/
*.har
*-status.json
omi_status.json
telemetry*.json

# working notes — my own tracking, not part of the project
.notes/
scratch/
scratchpad/

# build outputs
build/
build_ble/
*.uf2
*.hex
*.bin
*.elf
*.map
*.zip

# local tooling
.venv/
toolshim/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
